PARITY DECISION (documented — NOT a silent drift, covenant #9):
  The web line plots RAW °C while its axis label + reference lines are in the user's
  display unit — a latent °F scale mismatch in the web source. Per the repo SI-cutover
  policy ("read SI from the API, convert ONLY at the display boundary") and to agree with
  the reference lines, this port converts the line to the display unit too. In °C the
  conversion is the identity → byte-identical to the web; in °F it is the evidently-intended,
  self-consistent result. Recorded in TemperatureTrendChart.Adapter.swift header + plan.

