WHY DEFERRED (the failure PRE-EXISTS this change; ZERO TemperatureTrend errors):
  Both app targets fail to compile with, identically:
    apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/AcDcStatsPanel.Tests.swift:19:8:
      error: unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'    (+ `@testable import TeslaSync`)
  Root cause (structural, repo-wide): project.yml globs the whole `TeslaSync/feature-views`
  directory into the iOS/macOS APP targets, which sweeps every co-located `*.Tests.swift`
  (145 of them; tests are meant to live in the `Tests/Unit` XCTest target) into the app
  module. An app target cannot link `XCTest` nor `@testable import` itself. Confirmed by
  pbxproj membership analysis: TeslaSync & TeslaSync-macOS each list 145 *.Tests.swift +
  145 *.Previews.swift in their Sources phase. The build fails on AcDcStatsPanel.Tests.swift
  (alphabetically first) — a PRE-EXISTING SIBLING file, NOT TemperatureTrendChart — so the
  blocker is independent of this change. This is the repo's sanctioned "code-complete +
  DEFERRED full-app Xcode gate" disposition used by every P4 feature-view surface to date
  (92/92 prior logs: IOS_EXIT=65 / MAC_EXIT=65, DEFERRED). Wiring tests into the test target
  is the integration prompt's job, not this per-surface prompt (allowed files:
  TemperatureTrendChart.* + this log).

  Surface-level build proof in lieu of the contaminated full-app gate: the 6 source files
  compile cleanly (EXIT=0) against the real iPhoneSimulator26.5 SDK + real design tokens
  under Swift 6 / strict concurrency (see RUNNABLE HOST GATES above).

